  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "In North America, an owner evaluating **branded residences** should start with the strongest luxury and upper-upscale hotel brands: **Marriott** (especially **Ritz-Carlton** and **St. Regis**), **Four Seasons**, and **Trump** are the top brands in the region by completed and pipeline schemes.[3] Savills also identifies **Four Seasons, The Ritz-Carlton, and St. Regis** as the top hotel brands across the Americas.[1]\n\nBeyond those leaders, the main brands an owner should consider include **Accor** brands such as **Fairmont**, **Raffles**, and **Banyan Tree**; **Mandarin Oriental**; **Rosewood**; **Hyatt** brands such as **Park Hyatt**, **Andaz**, and **Grand Hyatt**; **IHG** brands such as **InterContinental** and **Regent**; **Hilton** brands such as **Waldorf Astoria** and **Conrad**; and resort/lifestyle operators such as **Aman**, **Six Senses**, **Kempinski**, **Banyan Group**, and **Kerzner**.[2][5][7][8]\n\nA practical way to think about the shortlist is:\n\n| Brand family | Why it matters for North America branded residences |\n|---|---|\n| **Marriott** | Broadest scale and strongest luxury-branded residence platforms, especially **Ritz-Carlton** and **St. Regis**.[1][3][15] |\n| **Four Seasons** | Consistently among the strongest luxury residence brands in the Americas.[1][3][8] |\n| **Accor** | Relevant through **Fairmont**, **Raffles**, and **Banyan Tree**.[2][5][7][8] |\n| **Mandarin Oriental** | High-end, globally recognized, especially for urban luxury projects.[7][8] |\n| **Rosewood** | Fast-growing luxury operator with strong pipeline momentum.[7][8] |\n| **Hyatt** | Useful for projects targeting upper-upscale to luxury buyers, especially **Park Hyatt**, **Andaz**, **Grand Hyatt**.[2][8] |\n| **IHG** | Most relevant through **InterContinental**, **Regent**, and **Six Senses**.[2][8] |\n| **Hilton** | Worth considering via **Waldorf Astoria** and **Conrad**.[4][8] |\n| **Aman / Banyan Group / Kerzner** | Best for ultra-luxury or resort-led developments.[2][8] |\n\nIf you want, I can also turn this into a **developer shortlist by project type**—for example, **urban luxury**, **resort**, or **ultra-luxury mixed-use** in North America.",
